  (text "CPU data pins CD0-CD7 carry the bank address while PHI2 is low.\nThe CPLD latches BA0-BA3 from CD0-CD3; the 74AHC245 is only enabled\n(BUF_OE low) while PHI2 is high, so the bank byte never reaches the\nsystem bus. RDY has a pull-up rather than a tie to +5V because WAI\ndrives it low. BE is held high; TIM-Bus DMA and INH are pulled up but\nnot used by this board. J1 brings out E (emulation mode) for debugging." (at 25.4 163.52 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 61765413-589f-4f88-a56f-3f8661cff427)
  )
)
